course: dictionary
lesson: 8840
title: Shipping: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shipping is a noun, and it is also the -ing form of the verb ship. Its main meaning is sending goods from one place to another, by sea, air, road or post. Use the words around it to work out which meaning fits.
explain: «In 1956 Malcom McLean started using standard shipping containers; today about four in five tonnes of world trade go by sea.» The sentence is about containers and trade, so shipping means sending goods, mostly by sea.
explain: Shipping can also mean the cost of sending things. On a shop website, «free shipping» means you do not pay extra to have your order sent. Check it: free shipping does not mean free ships!
explain: «The Strait of Dover ... is one of the busiest shipping lanes in the world.» Here shipping means the ships of a route. A lane is a path, so a shipping lane is a path that ships travel along. Swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: Shipping means sending goods from one place to another, by sea, air, road or post.
fact: Shipping can also mean the cost of sending things, as in «free shipping».
fact: Shipping can mean all the ships of an area, as in «shipping lanes», the routes ships travel along.
fact: Shipping is the -ing form of the verb ship, which means to send something.
fact: A strait is a narrow stretch of sea joining two larger bodies of water, and a few straits carry a large share of the world's shipping.
exercise: In «free shipping» on a shop website, what does shipping mean? | Going shopping by sea | A type of boat with a sail | *The cost of sending your order | The name of the shop
exercise: «The Strait of Dover is one of the busiest shipping lanes in the world.» What are shipping lanes? | Lanes in a swimming pool | Paths for walkers by the sea | Roads for lorries on land | *Routes that ships travel along
exercise: Which word is the -ing form of the verb ship, meaning sending something? | *Shipping | Ships | Shipped | Shipment
test: «A strait is a narrow stretch of sea joining two larger bodies of water.» What is a strait? | A cheap way to post parcels | A tall rock standing in the sea | A big ship with many containers | *A narrow stretch of sea joining two larger bodies of water
test: A parcel costs £3 for shipping. What does shipping mean here? | The name of the parcel company | *The cost of sending the parcel | The date the parcel arrives | A ship that carries parcels
exam: Which sentence uses shipping to mean the ships of an area? | She paid extra for shipping on her order | I will ship the box to my cousin tomorrow | *The shipping in the Strait of Malacca was busy all day | The shipping of parcels takes two days
